## Remaining Gaps and Risk Boundaries

The repo is strong, but the demo should be presented with these boundaries:

- Simulated results are not endpoint certification.
- CloudTrail data events are not complete HTTP transcripts.
- CloudTrail may omit headers, body details, and SDK-level behavior.
- Offline bucket config is user-supplied and must be trusted or independently
  collected.
- Lifecycle behavior is static-review only; time-based behavior is not proven.
- Performance, throughput, latency under load, and cost are not benchmarked.
- The tool does not prove IAM policy equivalence.
- The tool does not migrate data.
- The tool does not verify backup correctness.
- The tool does not prove application business criticality.
- The tool does not replace application integration testing.
- The corpus value depends on real redacted case contributions over time.

These are acceptable boundaries. They keep the product credible and focused.

